## Layer 5: Renderers

### Render modes (orthogonal to encoding tier)

```rust
enum RenderMode {
    Standard,   // Symbol-per-state, clean layout
    Dynamic,    // Cellular automaton effects, wavefront animation
    Compact,    // Single-line summary
}
```

### Terminal renderer

Carriage-return based (`\r` + `\x1b[{N}A` cursor-up). Zero dependencies.
Falls back to append-only when piped (not a TTY).

The terminal renderer implements FrameLoop:
- `update()`: processes observer events, advances animations, handles resize
- `render()`: walks DagLayout positions, writes symbols at each coordinate

The renderer doesn't compute layout — it receives a DagLayout and paints
symbols into it. If the viewport changes, it requests a new layout.

### Unified animation model

All animations — spinners, edge wavefronts, node morphs, cellular automaton
patterns — share the same underlying structure: a **SubDag with Frame nodes
and a Cycle edge**. The renderer advances frames; the animation type just
determines what the frame content is.

```rust
/// Single animation state, shared by ALL animation types.
struct Animation {
    frames: Vec<String>,     // Frame content (from SubDag Frame nodes)
    current: usize,          // Current frame index
    interval: Duration,      // Time between frames
    elapsed: Duration,       // Time since last frame advance
    mode: AnimationMode,     // How to loop
}

enum AnimationMode {
    Cycle,        // Loop forever (spinners, idle automaton)
    Once,         // Play once then hold last frame (node morph)
    Propagate {   // Advance position along a path (edge wavefront)
        path_len: usize,
        position: usize,
    },
}
```

This means:
- **Spinners** = Animation { frames: [🌑,🌒,🌓,🌔], mode: Cycle }
- **Node morph** = Animation { frames: [○,◔,◑,◐], mode: Once }
- **Edge wavefront** = Animation { frames: [═], mode: Propagate { path_len, .. } }
- **Idle automaton** = Animation { frames: [·pattern·], mode: Cycle }

No special cases. The `Animation` struct is the universal frame-cycling
primitive. Each animation type is just a different set of frames + mode
constructed from the same SymbolOp::Frame SubDags.

Frame scheduling uses Adaptive policy: slows for visually interesting
transitions, catches up when execution is fast. See Appendix C.

### CI renderer

CiProgressObserver wraps CiContext — formalizes existing ad-hoc callbacks.
Uses ASCII tier. Viewport: 120 cols, unbounded height, append-only.

### Web renderer (future, deferred)

DagProgress has Serialize → JSON/SSE to browser. Viewport from container
element. Zero changes to Layers 1-4 needed.

