## Key design decisions

- **Symbols in core/ir**: vocabulary not rendering engine; parallels
  language module; any crate can use without renderer dependency
- **Three tiers**: emoji default (we control env), unicode for edge cases,
  ASCII for CI/pipes — same vocab serves all contexts
- **Dynamic as RenderMode not Tier**: encoding (emoji/unicode/ascii) and
  temporal behavior (static/animated) are orthogonal dimensions
- **Carriage return not TUI**: zero deps, non-interactive, fixed-size
  display; DagProgress model supports swapping in TUI later
- **Observer not channel**: execution is synchronous single-threaded;
  observer is simpler; trait stays same if switching to channels later
- **Frame loop as trait**: decouples render timing from execution timing;
  same trait works for sync (between nodes) and async (own thread)
- **Frame policy choices**: Latest (never lag), Sequential (see everything),
  Adaptive (best of both) — renderer picks based on context
- **DagProgress separate from ExecutionLog**: live state machine vs post-hoc
  record; different concerns, don't couple them
- **Viewport as explicit type**: every renderer must provide one; layout
  adapts to constraints rather than assuming infinite space
- **DagLayout in core/ir not renderer crate**: it's a spatial projection of
  topology, not a rendering concern; any renderer can consume it
- **Three overflow strategies**: Collapse (priority-based hiding), Truncate
  (level cutoff), Scroll (focus tracking) — layout picks based on context

